A '''[[Confederal Convention]]''' took place in the [[District of Castejón]], [[Balisca]] from 17 June to 22 October 1883. The convention was the second to be held under the guise of amending the [[Compromise of 1827]], although the intention from the outset of many attending delegates was to create an entirely new system of Government rather than fix the existing one. Delegates representative of every region and territory across the Baliscan archipelago were in attendance. The delegates elected [[Ariranha]], a militant figure of the [[Cantonal War]] (and representing [[Jaguarundi]]) to become the {{W|Primus inter pares|''primus inter pares''}} of the convention. 

The result of the convention was the creation of the [[Constitution of Balisca|1883 Baliscan Constitution]], which established policies that tended toward a [[w:progressive politics|progressive]], [[W:Anti-clericalism|anti-clerical]] system of {{W|democratic socialism}}, including the {{W|separation of church and state}}, [[w:Self-governance|self-policing]], recognition of [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|indigenous sovereignty]], the remission of rent, the abolition of {{W|child labor}}, and the [[w:workers' self-management|right of employees to take over an enterprise]]. {{W|Feminist}}, {{W|socialist}}, [[w:Communism|communist]] and [[anarchism in Balisca|proto-anarchist]] currents significantly influenced the Convention. 

